---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets"
import CaseStudy from "@/layouts/case-study.astro"
import { getProject } from "@/data/projects"
import envelopeImg from "@/assets/projects/ncga-stationery/envelope-editor.png"

const project = getProject("ncga-stationery-templates")!

const pictureFormats: ("avif" | "webp")[] = ["avif", "webp"]
const pictureWidths = [640, 960, 1280]
const pictureSizes = "(min-width: 768px) 960px, 100vw"
---

<CaseStudy
  project={project}
  title="NCGA Stationery Template System"
  seoTitle="NCGA Stationery Template System · Information Architecture"
  seoDescription="Designing a constrained template engine for NCGA legislator letterhead and envelopes: LOCKED vs DATA-DRIVEN fields, print-accurate preview, and fewer production mistakes."
>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    The North Carolina General Assembly print shop produces official stationery
    for all 170 legislators. Each order follows the same formal brand guidelines,
    but requires distinct contact information, committee assignments, and chamber wording.
    Before this system, repeat orders relied on separate files for each member, allowing small
    discrepancies in spacing, ink color, and committee data to compound across all 170 profiles.
  </p>

  <h2>Locked vs. Data-Driven Fields</h2>
  <p>
    Production-approved variation lives in a typed <strong>LegislatorRecord</strong>,
    while core layout geometry and brand standards stay locked. <strong>Locked elements</strong>:
    the state seal, the official masthead, licensed typefaces, page grids, margins, and recycling mark geometry.
    <strong>Data-driven elements</strong>: member name, chamber, office address, phone number, committee list, and ink color, with visibility toggles that hide unused sections without deleting underlying data.
  </p>

  <div class="template-flow" aria-label="Legislator record to output">
    <div class="template-flow__node">
      <span>Input</span>
      <strong>LegislatorRecord</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="template-flow__connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="template-flow__node template-flow__node--wide">
      <span>Locked template</span>
      <strong>Seal, masthead, grid, type</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="template-flow__connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="template-flow__node">
      <span>Output</span>
      <strong>Letterhead or envelope PDF</strong>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Same Record, Different Surfaces</h2>
  <p>
    Letterhead and envelopes share a single underlying data model, but present tailored input forms. The envelope editor removes phone numbers and committee lists, omits the state seal to match production artwork, and restricts return addresses to official legislative buildings with fixed ZIP codes. Recipient addresses are left to a downstream mail merge.
  </p>

  <figure class="case-figure">
    <Picture
      src={envelopeImg}
      alt="Envelope editor with building picker and print-accurate envelope preview."
      formats={pictureFormats}
      widths={pictureWidths}
      sizes={pictureSizes}
    />
    <figcaption>
      Envelope surface: building picker instead of free-text address, no seal,
      recipients added later by mail merge.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Outcome</h2>
  <p>
    The browser preview renders in exact inches and points, while PDF output uses a second renderer that shares identical logic for chamber copy, ink colors, and visible committees. Personalized mailings to all 170 members now go out in one press pass instead of two.
  </p>
  <p>
    Related NCGA work not shown here includes a press-split calculator, identity
    systems, job tickets, proofing tools, and high-volume production workflows.
  </p>
</CaseStudy>

<style>
  .template-flow {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
  }

  .template-flow__node {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--background) 96%, var(--muted));
  }

  .template-flow__node span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .template-flow__node strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .template-flow__connector {
    width: 1px;
    height: 1.25rem;
    margin-left: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--border);
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .template-flow {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 2rem minmax(0, 1.2fr) 2rem minmax(
          0,
          1fr
        );
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0;
    }

    .template-flow__connector {
      width: 100%;
      height: 1px;
      margin-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
